  "description": "An updated Colonial on a quiet street in historic Mount Holly, with 2,612 square feet spread across three levels. The entry foyer opens to flexible space that suits a reading nook or a home office, and the living and dining areas run together into the kitchen. That kitchen carries white shaker soft-close cabinetry, granite counters, a large double island with seating, stainless appliances, and pendant and recessed lighting over a decorative tile backsplash. Hardwood runs through the main level. Three bedrooms and two full baths sit on the first upper floor with a fourth bedroom above, and there is a powder room on the main level. Outside there is a deck and a 0.14-acre lot with alley parking in addition to the driveway. Radiator heat on natural gas, ductless mini-split cooling, public water and sewer. Close to downtown Mount Holly, shopping, dining, parks and public transportation.",
